English (reference translation)
======================================================================

1. Scope

   "The Software" means everything in this repository (source code, resources, assets such
   as icons, build configuration, documentation) and the "Volace" app built from it,
   including APK / AAB files. "The Owner" means the copyright holder named above.

2. What is permitted

   The Owner grants you a free, non-exclusive permission to do the following, and only the
   following:

   (a) view the source code of the Software;
   (b) use the "Volace" app;
   (c) build the app yourself from the source code in this repository and use that build
       for your own personal use.

3. What is not permitted

   Everything not listed in section 2 is not permitted. In particular (these are examples,
   not a complete list):

   - modifying or adapting the Software, or creating derivative works, including
     modifications for personal use;
   - distributing, publishing or redistributing copies of the Software (source code, build
     outputs or assets), whether original or modified, free of charge or for a fee;
   - selling the Software, providing it for a fee, redistributing it commercially, or
     distributing it through any store (including Google Play) or website by anyone
     other than the Owner;
   - incorporating any part of the Software (code, icons or other assets) into other
     software or works;
   - handing a build made under 2(c) to anyone else.

   A permission not written in this license is valid only if the Owner expressly gives it,
   for example in writing.

4. The Owner's rights and the official release

   All rights in the Software other than those granted here are reserved by the Owner.
   Nothing in this license prevents the Owner from distributing an official release of the
   Software on Google Play or elsewhere, including for a fee. The price and terms of an
   official release are those shown by the store, and do not affect the permission in 2(c),
   which is free of charge.

5. Public repository and GitHub

   This repository is public on GitHub. To the extent the GitHub Terms of Service allow
   others to view a public repository and to fork it on GitHub (reproduction on GitHub
   within GitHub's functionality), this license does not restrict that. Any other use,
   even of a fork, is limited to what this license permits.

6. Third-party materials

   The Software includes or uses third-party assets and libraries, which are governed by
   their own licenses (see THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md). The restrictions of this license do not
   limit the rights those third-party licenses give you.

7. Rights under law

   This license does not limit any right that cannot be limited under applicable law (such
   as uses permitted by statutory exceptions to copyright).

8. No warranty; limitation of liability

   The Software is provided "as is", without warranty of any kind, express or implied. To
   the extent permitted by law, the Owner is not liable for any damage arising from the use
   of, or inability to use, the Software.

9. Termination

   If you violate the terms of this license, the permission granted to you ends
   automatically.
